## Why This Is Asked
Real-time pipelines present subtle consistency and resilience challenges that unit tests alone cannot catch. Interviewers want to see that you understand end-to-end testing across distributed systems, including CI/CD integration.

## Key Concepts
- Exactly-once semantics via transactional sinks and checkpointing
- Stateful stream processing and its failure modes
- Backward/forward schema evolution to prevent consumer breakage
- Backpressure handling, failure recovery, and replay safety
- Observability within CI/CD pipelines

## Code Example
```javascript
// Verify exactly-once processing with idempotent writes
const result = await warehouse.query(`
  SELECT event_id, COUNT(*) as score_count
  FROM risk_scores
  GROUP BY event_id
  HAVING COUNT(*) > 1
`);
assert(result.length === 0, 'Duplicate events detected');

// Validate replay safety after simulated outage
await kafka.broker.crash({ node: 3 });
await flink.restartFromCheckpoint();
const postRecoveryScores = await warehouse.fetchLatestScores();
assert(postRecoveryScores.length === expectedCount);
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end reliability of streaming reconciliation systems, focusing on critical aspects like idempotency, exactly-once semantics, drift detection, and rollback mechanisms under high throughput conditions—essential for fintech and large-scale payment systems.

## Key Concepts
- End-to-end testing in streaming pipelines
- Idempotent reconciliation and exactly-once semantics
- Drift detection and rollback/replay strategies
- Test data generation for duplicates and out-of-order events
- Performance validation at scale (1M events/sec)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: synthetic event generator with duplicates
function genEvents(n){
  const events=[];
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    events.push({id: i, timestamp: Date.now(), amount: Math.random()*1000});
    if(Math.random()<0.1) events.push(events[events.length-1]); // 10% duplicates
  }
  return events.sort(() => Math.random()-0.5); // Shuffle for out-of-order
}
```

